Grow memDecompress()'s zstd output buffer as the data is decoded
instead of sizing it from the frame header.

do_memDecompress() (src/main/connections.c) sized the zstd output
buffer from ZSTD_getFrameContentSize() on the first frame and
decompressed in one call.  That size comes from the input and is not
checked against the data, so a 10-byte truncated frame claiming
3.96 GiB made R allocate 3.96 GiB before zstd reported "Src size is
incorrect", and input with more than one frame (valid zstd, e.g.
concatenated .zst files) failed with "Destination buffer is too small".
Start no larger than 3 * the input size, as the gzip, bzip2 and xz
branches do, and retry with a doubled buffer on
ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall, which zstd reports only when the decoded
data overflows the buffer (a lying header gives "Data corruption
detected").  Each attempt starts afresh, so the previous buffer is
released with vmaxset().

Found by OSS-Fuzz (libFuzzer_r_decompress): testcase 5388943009579008,
a reproducible Out-of-memory (malloc of 4.2 GB against the 2560 MB
limit) on an 11-byte input reaching zstd through type = "unknown".
The path became reachable when trunk started requiring libzstd
(r90802, built from source here since PR #83).

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #455, filed 2026-11-05 (no Bugzilla report).  The upstream PR also adds a
regression test to tests/reg-tests-1e.R, left out here so this carry
patch does not go stale with that file.
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk.

diff --git a/src/main/connections.c b/src/main/connections.c
index 25b4bd92ec..21dd031720 100644
--- a/src/main/connections.c
+++ b/src/main/connections.c
@@ -2413,6 +2413,7 @@ static unsigned long long ZSTD_decompressBound(const void* src, size_t srcSize)
 #endif
 
 #include <zstd.h>
+#include <zstd_errors.h> /* ZSTD_getErrorCode; older zstd.h lacks it */
 
 typedef struct zstdfileconn {
     FILE *fp;
@@ -7490,8 +7491,24 @@ do_memDecompress(SEXP call, SEXP op, SEXP args, SEXP env)
 	    outlen = ZSTD_decompressBound(p, inlen);
 	if (outlen == ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_ERROR)
 	    error("internal error in memDecompress(%s)", "type = \"zstd\"");
-	buf = (Bytef *) R_alloc(outlen, sizeof(Bytef));
-	res = ZSTD_decompress(buf, outlen, p, inlen);
+	/* The size in the frame header is not checked against the data and
+	   covers only the first frame, so start no larger than the other
+	   types do and grow the buffer when the output does not fit.  Each
+	   attempt starts afresh, so the previous buffer can be released. */
+	if (outlen > 3*inlen)
+	    outlen = 3*inlen;
+	const void *vmax = vmaxget();
+	while(1) {
+	    vmaxset(vmax);
+	    buf = (Bytef *) R_alloc(outlen, sizeof(Bytef));
+	    res = ZSTD_decompress(buf, outlen, p, inlen);
+	    if (ZSTD_getErrorCode(res) == ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall
+		&& outlen < SIZE_MAX/2) {
+		outlen = (outlen < 3*inlen) ? 3*inlen : 2*outlen;
+		continue;
+	    }
+	    break;
+	}
 	if (ZSTD_isError(res))
 	    error("internal error in memDecompress(%s)", ZSTD_getErrorName(res));
 	ans = allocVector(RAWSXP, res);
